ty":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.003709256591626833,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":15.2,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.010035865573805869,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":62.5,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.031920273348519365,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":46.8,"_gate_insider_own":0.05328,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":35.5,"_gate_insider_buying":0.286,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":28.6,"pf":[],"description_full":"Triumph Financial, Inc., a financial holding company, provides banking, factoring, payments, and intelligence services in the United States. It offers deposit products, including checking, savings, money market, and certificates of deposit; and loan products, such as commercial real estate, commercial construction, land, and land development, residential real estate, agriculture, and consumer loans, as well as commercial and industrial loans, equipment loans, asset-based loans, business loans for working capital and operational purposes, and liquid credit loans. The company also provides electronic banking services, debit cards, insurance brokerage services, mortgage warehouse facilities, and transportation factoring services; payment, audit, and other banking services for the over the road trucking industry; and LoadPay product, a digital bank account developed for Carriers, as well as provides service and performance scoring and benchmarking to the over-the-road trucking industry. The company was formerly known as Triumph Bancorp, Inc. and changed its name to Triumph Financial, Inc. in December 2022. Triumph Financial, Inc. was incorporated in 2003 and is headquartered in Dallas, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Aaron P. Graft J.D. | Founder, Vice Chairman, President & CEO | Age 47 | Compensation: $1.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $305K ranks in the bottom quartile among Financial Services peers, improving at 14%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $10K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Triumph Financial, Inc. is a small-cap financial services business with a $1.5B market cap on $439M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -3% over the past three years and +13% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 8% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 0.4\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.4%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 5.3% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.3\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 195% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.9528777316051886},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.4) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Financial Services peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 22% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (11.3% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Among the least levered in Financial Services \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Is Triumph Financial (TFIN) Below Fair Value After Its Stronger 2026 Results?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/banks/nyse-tfin/triumph-financial/news/is-triumph-financial-tfin-below-fair-value-after-its-stronge","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793794774.999,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.975,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"(TFIN) Movement Within Algorithmic Entry Frameworks","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/23/TFIN_Movement_Within_Algorithmic_Entry_Frameworks_110326090001_1793757601.html","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793757601.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.477,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Triumph Financial (TFIN) Stock Could Be 33% Overvalued After Strong Q3 Results","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/banks/nyse-tfin/triumph-financial/news/triumph-financial-tfin-stock-could-be-33-overvalued-after-st","date":"2026-11-02","timestamp":1